# React (Vite)

- **One component per file**; colocate only tiny private helpers with the component.
- **Reuse**: Shared UI under `apps/web/src/components`; hooks under `apps/web/src/hooks`; API under `apps/web/src/lib`.
- **shadcn/ui**: Primitives live in `src/components/ui/*` (registry output). Prefer composing those over one-off styled elements; keep feature UI in barrel folders under `components/` or `pages/`.
- **Tailwind**: Utility-first styling; mobile-first breakpoints (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).
- **A11y**: Semantic HTML, labels, keyboard focus for interactive elements.
- **No `alert()`**: Never use `alert()`, `confirm()`, or `prompt()`. Use the shadcn/ui `Dialog` component (or `AlertDialog` for confirmations) instead.
- **Forms**: Use **react-hook-form** (`useForm`, `Controller`, `FormProvider`) for all forms — no uncontrolled `useState` fields or bare `<form>` wiring. Pair with **zod** + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` for schema validation. Surface field errors via the shadcn/ui `FormField` / `FormMessage` primitives. Only use plain controlled inputs for trivially single-field, stateless UI (e.g. an isolated search box with no submission).
